+# Docs Feedback Design
+
+## Summary
+
+ForkMesh docs will collect anonymous first-party feedback through a D1-backed `feedback` table.
+The existing "Was this page helpful?" buttons on the docs page will become functional.
+A "Yes" click records a positive vote immediately.
+A "No" click opens a small modal with an optional free-text improvement field, and the dislike is recorded even when the field is empty.
+
+## Goals
+
+Record whether docs readers click like or dislike.
+Preserve optional qualitative feedback for dislike clicks.
+Keep the feature anonymous and lightweight.
+Avoid making the docs page feel broken if feedback submission fails.
+Prevent an unauthenticated endpoint from growing D1 without bounds.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+This feature will not require login.
+This feature will not attach account identity.
+This feature will not build an admin analytics dashboard in the first pass.
+This feature will not modify generated changelog files.
+
+## Data Model
+
+Add a D1 table named `feedback`.
+
+The table will store one row per submitted feedback event.
+Fields will include an auto-incrementing `id`, timestamp `ts`, `source`, `vote`, `path`, optional `message`, `ip_hash`, and `user_agent`.
+The `source` for the docs page will be `docs`.
+The `vote` will be either `like` or `dislike`.
+The `message` will be stored only after sanitization and length capping.
+The raw client IP will not be stored.
+Instead, the Worker will derive a stable hash from the Cloudflare connecting IP using server-side key material.
+If the IP header or key material is unavailable, `ip_hash` will be stored as an empty string.
+
+The table will be bounded by keeping only the most recent feedback rows.
+This matches existing anonymous intake patterns in the Worker, such as installer diagnostics and telemetry.
+
+## API
+
+Add `POST /api/feedback`.
+
+The request body will accept JSON with `source`, `vote`, `path`, and optional `message`.
+The endpoint will reject unsupported HTTP methods.
+The endpoint will validate `source` and `vote`.
+The endpoint will sanitize `path`, `message`, and `user_agent` before storage.
+Malformed submissions will return a normal client error.
+Storage failures will not expose internal details.
+
+The response for a valid submission will be `{"ok": true}` with `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+
+## Frontend Behavior
+
+The docs page will keep its current "Was this page helpful?" placement and visual style.
+The "Yes" button will submit a `like` event immediately.
+The "No" button will open a modal asking what was confusing, missing, or could be improved.
+The textarea will be optional.
+Submitting the modal will record a `dislike` event with the optional text.
+Closing the modal without submitting will not send a feedback row.
+The user can still submit a dislike with an empty message.
+
+After a successful submit, the UI will show a short "Thanks" state.
+If the request fails, the UI will fail quietly and restore the buttons so the reader can continue using the page.
+The implementation will not use local duplicate suppression in the first pass, so each intentional click submission becomes one row.
+
+## Error Handling and Abuse Controls
+
+The endpoint will cap request body size before parsing.
+The message length will be capped.
+The path and source strings will be capped.
+The user agent will be capped.
+The table will be pruned after inserts to keep only the most recent feedback rows.
+No raw IP address, email address, account name, or authenticated user record will be stored by this feature.
+
+## Testing
+
+Static docs tests will verify the feedback buttons have stable data hooks, the dislike modal exists, and the page posts to `/api/feedback`.
+Schema tests will verify the `feedback` table DDL exists in `SCHEMA_STATEMENTS`.
+A migration test or file presence check will verify there is a D1 migration for the feedback table.
+Worker tests will cover feedback payload normalization for valid likes, valid dislikes with and without message text, invalid votes, length caps, and body-size rejection behavior where practical.
-- 
