+# Docs Feedback Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Build anonymous first-party docs feedback capture with durable D1 storage and an optional dislike feedback modal.
+
+**Architecture:** The docs page posts feedback events to a new unauthenticated Worker endpoint at `/api/feedback`.
+The Worker validates and sanitizes the payload, stores one row per click in a bounded `feedback` D1 table, and hashes the client IP with the existing `blind_index` HMAC helper instead of storing raw IP.
+The frontend keeps the existing docs footer placement and adds a small modal only for dislike details.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Cloudflare Python Worker, D1 SQL migrations, static HTML with page-local JavaScript, pytest source-contract and AST-isolated unit tests.
+
+---
+
+## File Structure
+
+- `src/entry.py`: Add feedback constants, pure payload normalizers, `feedback_handler`, and the `/api/feedback` route branch.
+- `src/schema.py`: Add idempotent D1 DDL for the `feedback` table and indexes.
+- `migrations/0026_feedback.sql`: Add the file-based migration equivalent of the schema DDL.
+- `tests/test_feedback.py`: Add AST-isolated tests for payload normalization plus source-contract tests for route registration, IP hashing, schema DDL, and migration parity.
+- `tests/test_docs_frontend.py`: Extend existing docs shell tests to pin feedback hooks, modal markup, and `/api/feedback` posting.
+- `public/docs/index.html`: Wire the visible docs feedback UI and modal.
+- `public/docs.html`: Keep the legacy docs URL byte-for-byte aligned with `public/docs/index.html`.
+
